{"title":"2014 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb60e0857a2c0a2c47acfbe81781032feb1f7150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/3/a838d1282524b78e2dfc9f92bac35993353c2015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-d \\ge 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" /> and all zeros <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/4/b44a208581b717c11e38b8648c16ab860a0de926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2, x_3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/420543d9a4f93ed4180b45b3149b663a8aa7674d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> of the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/f/a1f48d460b948f0519285e04b172663690cc812d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)=x^4+ax^3+bx^2+cx+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"252\" height=\"21\" /> are real. Find the smallest value the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/b/24b600224dbe28e2099d79b7fee41ab6f1483f07.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x_1^2+1)(x_2^2+1)(x_3^2+1)(x_4^2+1)\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"19\" /> can take.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d4023589a374e5b4a1bc6063d887aec205e0d3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of integers. Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d0760c95af6e8959fada128e407a3667ffdf9676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f : \\mathbb{Z} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/a/d8a096b16717c78172a9998a3e34284f510e5049.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xf(2f(y)-x)+y^2f(2x-f(y))=\\frac{(f(x))^2}{x}+f(yf(y))\\]\" width=\"426\" height=\"39\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/376866868713b9b86be09ca29980f9e0f7c9a43f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d79c96e270e148516fb5dd4a73725d8be87c80c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Prove that there exists an infinite set of points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b1a20529975d46579986b86a5706fa36bda7794.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\ldots,\\,\\,\\,\\,P_{-3},\\,\\,\\,\\,P_{-2},\\,\\,\\,\\,P_{-1},\\,\\,\\,\\,P_0,\\,\\,\\,\\,P_1,\\,\\,\\,\\,P_2,\\,\\,\\,\\,P_3,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\ldots\\]\" width=\"369\" height=\"16\" /> in the plane with the following property: For any three distinct integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b28547efd22be1c4a05fa193cd7038fc65d71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d874e17c7ea25b97dc858c88374b891b2a6f6d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/15245bc6e388de68e6fa07b00f49b5386c770d5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe288e3048ab6eaa4dd26fe6b67f9a8ccc7ebfc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> are collinear if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/c/09cd6531601061be4c3add1cb888100be8bd132a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=2014$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"130\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be a positive integer. Two players <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> play a game on an infinite grid of regular hexagons. Initially all the grid cells are empty. Then the players alternately take turns with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> moving first. In his move, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> may choose two adjacent hexagons in the grid which are empty and place a counter in both of them. In his move, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> may choose any counter on the board and remove it. If at any time there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive grid cells in a line all of which contain a counter, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> wins. Find the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> cannot win in a finite number of moves, or prove that no such minimum value exists.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle with orthocenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the second intersection of the circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/2/1c2fc72679a58a713c8395c204bfd684d8d3b1f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AHC$\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> with the internal bisector of the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the circumcenter of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92b38136cabb69ee2f7b5711190e0042354f3419.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> the orthocenter of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d91d2a29d7b4556be19a003b0f830b700cdf92d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.  Prove that the length of segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to the circumradius of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Prove that there is a constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/b/c1bb51afff5fb240f36891f4551733ba8a674630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> with the following property: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e4211b2769e07903568a3bb3e0fd9e52a113cf85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> are positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a28370845df4646c9a8741723cc5beb04c2a5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(a+i, b+j)&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ff09116fe0cd1be9000acb1d03cc4599dce45c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i, j\\in\\{0, 1, \\ldots n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />, then<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02b7074a6db67693e1ca47702b4fe57d70147d3a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\min\\{a, b\\}&gt;c^n\\cdot n^{\\frac{n}{2}}.\\]\" width=\"154\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO\" title=\"2014 USAMO\">2014 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2014\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2013 USAMO Problems\">2013 USAMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2015 USAMO Problems\">2015 USAMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017235212\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 267/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1273/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 82/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7819/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.672      1 -total\n 57.99%    7.349      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 40.32%    5.109      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12652:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017235212 and revision id 215467. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}